  "correction_rules": [
    "Bias correction: Model consistently underestimates prices in early forecast periods; adjust downward by 0.5–1.5% for first 5–7 days if sentiment is neutral or slightly positive.",
    "Lag correction: Forecast often lags true price movements by 1–3 days; apply a 1-day forward shift for price spikes or sharp reversals.",
    "Overshoot correction: After price spikes (e.g., >65), model tends to overcorrect downward; reduce forecast by 1–2% in subsequent days to avoid premature correction.",
    "Mean reversion bias: Model overreacts to short-term volatility; apply smoothing filter (e.g., 3-day moving average) to forecast if sentiment is low or neutral.",
    "Sentiment-driven adjustment: If sentiment > 0.25, increase forecast by 0.5–1.0% for next 3–5 days to capture bullish momentum; if sentiment < 0.0, reduce by 0.5–1.0% to reflect bearish bias."
  ]
}
